  },
  data: {
    LLM: '1. Pegging Phase: Starting with the non-dealer, players play one tile at a time, keeping a running total of the pips (0-31 limit). Points scored for reaching exactly 15 or 31, and for sequences or blocks of same-value tiles.\n2. The Show: After pegging, players score their remaining 4 tiles + the starter tile for combinations.\n3. The Crib: The dealer scores the 4 discarded tiles + the starter tile.',
    Player: '1. Pegging Phase: Starting with the non-dealer, players play one tile at a time, keeping a running total of the pips (0-31 limit). Points scored for reaching exactly 15 or 31, and for sequences or blocks of same-value tiles.\n2. The Show: After pegging, players score their remaining 4 tiles + the starter tile for combinations.\n3. The Crib: The dealer scores the 4 discarded tiles + the starter tile.',
    objective: 'Be the first to reach 61 or 121 points on the cribbage board.',
    gameplay: '1. Pegging Phase: Starting with the non-dealer, players play one tile at a time, keeping a running total of the pips (0-31 limit). Points scored for reaching exactly 15 or 31, and for sequences or blocks of same-value tiles.\n2. The Show: After pegging, players score their remaining 4 tiles + the starter tile for combinations.\n3. The Crib: The dealer scores the 4 discarded tiles + the starter tile.',
    keyRules: [
      'The value of a tile is the SUM of its two ends (e.g., 5-3 = 8).',
      'Blank tiles (0-0) are valid and have value 0 for sums and sequences.',
      "Rules for 'Go' and '31' are identical to card cribbage.",
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: 'Two players. One is designated the dealer, the other the non-dealer; they exchange roles after each hand. All 28 tiles are mixed, each player draws six tiles, then each discards two face down into the crib.',
      deck: 'A standard set of 28 double-six dominoes.',
      equipment: 'Dominoes, Cribbage board (or score sheet).',
      dealing: "All 28 tiles are face-down and shuffled. Each player draws 6 tiles. Two from each hand are discarded into a four-tile 'Crib' belonging to the dealer. One tile is turned over from the boneyard as the 'Starter'.",
    },
    turnFlow: '1. Pegging Phase: Starting with the non-dealer, players play one tile at a time, keeping a running total of the pips (0-31 limit). Points scored for reaching exactly 15 or 31, and for sequences or blocks of same-value tiles.\n2. The Show: After pegging, players score their remaining 4 tiles + the starter tile for combinations.\n3. The Crib: The dealer scores the 4 discarded tiles + the starter tile.',
